From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] input: fts_touch: wake on a double tap while the screen is off

On Android the touch bus goes to the ADSP while the screen is off, and the
ADSP detects taps. Linux has no ADSP touch support, and the controller's
own gesture mode does not report a double tap with this firmware (tested:
no interrupt with the panel on or off). Normal touch reporting does keep
working with the panel powered off.

Add a double_tap_wake sysfs switch. When it is set, screen off keeps the
controller scanning (mutual sense only) with the bus and the interrupt on
the AP, and the interrupt armed as a wakeup source (GPIO 9 has a PDC
wake line). The interrupt handler reads the FIFO without a bus reference
and feeds the touch events to a small double tap detector, which reports
KEY_POWER; Phosh turns the screen on for the power key. Touches are not
reported while the screen is off. System suspend defers the interrupt
until the SPI bus has resumed, like the phone call mode does. Screen on
disarms the detector and resumes as before, without the ADSP bus request.

---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/fts_touch/fts.h	2026-10-23 17:06:01.941784138 +0100
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/fts_touch/fts.h	2026-10-23 17:07:08.484779845 +0100
@@ -397,6 +397,17 @@
   *                       from the host \n
   * - tbn             Touch Bus Negotiator context
   */
+/* Double tap detector state, used while the screen is off (tap to wake) */
+struct fts_tap_wake {
+	unsigned long fingers;	/* touch IDs currently down */
+	bool valid;		/* the current touch can still be a tap */
+	int taps;		/* taps completed in the current sequence */
+	ktime_t down_time;	/* when the current touch started */
+	ktime_t up_time;	/* when the first tap ended */
+	int x, y;		/* where the current touch started */
+	int first_x, first_y;	/* where the first tap started */
+};
+
